        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: réagir",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "réagir — \"to react\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Comment as-tu réagi quand tu as appris la nouvelle? How did you react when you heard the news?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Réagir à quelque chose. A -ir verb like finir."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "réagir is built from ré- \"back\" and agir \"to act\", which comes from Latin agere \"to do, to drive\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
